            "Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) restricts system authorization based on organizational roles assigned to users, while Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC) evaluates dynamic attributes (user role, resource sensitivity, client IP, time of day) through declarative security policy engines to enforce fine-grained least-privilege access."
